# Frontend environment. Copy to frontend/.env.local for local overrides.
#
# ONLY VITE_-prefixed variables belong here.
#
# Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into the client bundle as plain text.
# Anything in this file is therefore PUBLIC — visible to anyone who opens
# devtools. Never put an API key, token, or secret here, even temporarily.
#
# Backend secrets (GOOGLE_API_KEY and friends) live in the ROOT .env.example
# and are set on the backend host (Render), never on Vercel. This file exists
# partly so Vercel's import scan finds a correctly scoped set of variables
# here rather than falling back to the repo-root .env.example and offering
# you a backend-only secret.

# Base URL of the Reqoncile API.
# Local dev: leave unset — vite.config.js proxies /api to localhost:8000.
# Deployed:  set to the Render service URL, e.g. https://reqoncile-api.onrender.com
VITE_API_BASE=
